{"id":3851,"path":"/grammar-points/a1/at-in-on-prepositions-time/","parentId":540,"order":80,"section":"grammar-points","level":"a1","depth":3,"title":"At, in, on: Prepositions of time","seo":{"title":"At, in, on: Prepositions of time - Test-English","description":"Learn how to use 'at', 'in' and 'on' for time in this A1 Elementary grammar lesson. Clear rules, grammar charts and exercises. Practise now!","image":"/media/uploads/A1%E2%80%93Grammar_at-in-on_time.png"},"modified":"2026-02-18T10:39:00","kind":"lesson","parts":["<h3>Exercise 1</h3> <h5>Choose <em>at, in, on</em> to complete the sentences.</h5> <div data-quiz=\"441\"></div>","<h3>Exercise 2</h3> <h5>Choose the correct prepositions of time (at, in, on) to complete the sentences.</h5> <div data-quiz=\"442\"></div>","<h3>Exercise 3</h3> <h5>Complete the sentences using the correct prepositions of time: <em>at, in, on</em>.</h5> <div data-quiz=\"443\"></div>"],"explanation":"<p><img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-22903\" src=\"/media/uploads/at-in-on_time_new.png\" alt=\"Detailed grammar chart explaining the use of time prepositions 'at', 'in', and 'on' with examples for days, months, seasons, years, and specific times of day.\" width=\"500\" height=\"500\" loading=\"lazy\"></p> <h6></h6> <h3><strong>At</strong></h3> <p>Use <strong>at</strong> with times of day, including mealtimes, bedtime, etc.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><span><strong><em>at</em></strong></span><em> 3 o’clock, <span><strong>at</strong></span> 10.30 am, <span><strong>at</strong></span> noon, <span><strong>at</strong></span> dinnertime, <span><strong>at</strong></span> bedtime, <span><strong>at</strong></span> sunrise, <span><strong>at</strong></span> sunset, <span><strong>at</strong></span> the moment</em></li> </ul> <p>Use <strong>at</strong> in the following common expressions:</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><span><strong>at </strong></span>the weekend: <em>I don’t usually work <strong><span>at</span></strong> the weekend.</em></li> <li><span><strong>at </strong></span>Christmas/Easter: <em>I stay with my family <span><strong>at</strong></span> Christmas.</em></li> <li><span><strong>at </strong></span>the same time<strong>:</strong> <em>We finished the test <span><strong>at</strong></span> the same time.</em></li> <li><span><strong>at </strong></span>present/<span><strong>at</strong></span> the moment<strong>:</strong> <em>He’s not home <span><strong>at</strong></span> present. Try later.</em></li> </ul> <h3><strong>In</strong></h3> <p>Use <strong>in</strong> with <a href=\"/vocabulary/a1/days-months-seasons-a1-english-vocabulary/\">months, seasons</a>, years, decades, centuries and long periods of time in general.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><span><strong><em>in</em></strong></span><em> May, <span><strong>in</strong></span> the summer, <span><strong>in</strong></span> 1990, <span><strong>in</strong></span> the 1990s, <span><strong>in</strong></span> the 20th century, <span><strong>in</strong></span> the Ice Age, <span><strong>in</strong></span> the past/future</em></li> </ul> <h3><strong>On</strong></h3> <p>Use <strong>on</strong> followed by days and dates.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><span><strong><em>on</em></strong></span><em> Sunday, <span><strong>on</strong></span> Tuesday mornings, <span><strong>on</strong></span> 6 March, <span><strong>on</strong></span> 25 December 2010, <span><strong>on</strong></span> Christmas Day, <span><strong>on</strong></span> Independence Day, <span><strong>on</strong></span> my birthday, <span><strong>on</strong></span> New Year’s Eve</em></li> </ul> <h3>Parts of the day:</h3> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><span><strong>in</strong></span> the morning</li> <li><span><strong>in</strong></span> the afternoon</li> <li><span><strong>in</strong></span> the evening</li> <li><span><strong>at</strong></span> night</li> </ul> <h3><strong>Last</strong>, <strong>next</strong>, <strong>every</strong> and <strong>this</strong></h3> <p>When we say&nbsp;<strong>last, next, every, this</strong>,&nbsp;we do not use&nbsp;<strong>at, in, on</strong>.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>I went to London&nbsp;<span><strong>last</strong></span></em>&nbsp;<em>June</em>. <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21425\" src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></li> <li><em>I went to London <span><strong>in last</strong></span></em>&nbsp;<em>June</em>. <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21426\" src=\"/media/uploads/wrong.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></li> <li><em>He’s coming back&nbsp;<span><strong>next</strong></span></em> Tuesday.&nbsp;<img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21425\" src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></li> <li><em>He’s coming back <span><strong>on next</strong></span></em> Tuesday.&nbsp;<img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21426\" src=\"/media/uploads/wrong.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></li> <li><em>I go home&nbsp;<span><strong>every</strong></span>&nbsp;Easter.</em>&nbsp;<img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21425\" src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></li> <li><em>I go home <span><strong>at every</strong></span>&nbsp;Easter.</em>&nbsp;<img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21426\" src=\"/media/uploads/wrong.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></li> <li><em>We’ll call you&nbsp;<span><strong>this</strong></span>&nbsp;evening.</em>&nbsp;<img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21425\" src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></li> <li><em>We’ll call you <span><strong>in this</strong></span>&nbsp;evening.</em>&nbsp;<img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21426\" src=\"/media/uploads/wrong.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></li> </ul>","quizzes":[{"id":441,"questions":[{"id":3830,"num":"1","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>See you <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> Friday. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["in","at","on"]}]},{"id":3831,"num":"2","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>I brush my teeth <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> the morning. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["at","on","in"]}]},{"id":3832,"num":"3","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>The match is <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> 4 o'clock. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["in","at","on"]}]},{"id":3833,"num":"4","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>We have lunch <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> midday. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["in","at","on"]}]},{"id":3834,"num":"5","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>I'm busy <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> the moment.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["on","at","in"]}]},{"id":3835,"num":"6","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>My parents always visit me <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> my birthday. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["in","at","on"]}]},{"id":3836,"num":"7","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>He was born <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> the 19th century</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["in","on","at"]}]},{"id":3837,"num":"8","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>He usually goes on holiday <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> July</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["on","at","in"]}]},{"id":3838,"num":"9","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>They always get together <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> Christmas.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["on","at","in"]}]},{"id":3839,"num":"10","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>You can come <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> the weekend. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["in","at"]}]}]},{"id":442,"questions":[{"id":3840,"num":"1","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>I have to meet the clients _____ lunchtime. </div>","choices":[{"id":5823,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>at</span>"},{"id":5824,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>in</span>"},{"id":5825,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>on</span>"}]},{"id":3841,"num":"2","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>This happened _____ the 80s.</div>","choices":[{"id":5826,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>at </span>"},{"id":5827,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>in</span>"},{"id":5828,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>on</span>"}]},{"id":3842,"num":"3","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>We want to go for a drink after the concert _____ Friday evening</div>","choices":[{"id":5829,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>at</span>"},{"id":5830,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>in</span>"},{"id":5831,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>on</span>"}]},{"id":3843,"num":"4","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>You can plant these flowers _____ the autumn.</div>","choices":[{"id":5850,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>at</span>"},{"id":5851,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>in</span>"},{"id":5852,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>on</span>"}]},{"id":3844,"num":"5","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>Is your neighbourhood quiet _____ night?</div>","choices":[{"id":5832,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>at</span>"},{"id":5833,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>in</span>"},{"id":5834,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>on</span>"}]},{"id":3845,"num":"6","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>I will retire _____ 2030.</div>","choices":[{"id":5835,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>at</span>"},{"id":5836,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>in</span>"},{"id":5837,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>on</span>"}]},{"id":3846,"num":"7","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>My birthday is _____ the 10th of January. </div>","choices":[{"id":5838,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>at</span>"},{"id":5839,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>in</span>"},{"id":5840,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>on</span>"}]},{"id":3847,"num":"8","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>I usually go to bed _____ midnight. </div>","choices":[{"id":5841,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>at</span>"},{"id":5842,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>in</span>"},{"id":5843,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>on</span>"}]},{"id":3848,"num":"9","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>I don't work _____ Christmas day. </div>","choices":[{"id":5844,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>at</span>"},{"id":5845,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>in</span>"},{"id":5